@startuml detection
title US-03: Detection - Signal Loss Identified

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}" as AlertState
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

note over Evaluator
  Only the elected leader instance
  runs evaluation. Followers are
  on standby. (ADR-005)
end note

loop every 10s (scheduled scan)
  Evaluator -> Redis : SCAN entity:live:* + HGETALL each key
  Redis --> Evaluator : { entity_id, last_seen_ms, lat, lon } for all live entities

  note over Redis
    Detection is driven by last_seen_ms in the hash,
    not by TTL expiry. The key may still be alive
    when the threshold is crossed.
    TTL = SIGNAL_LOSS_THRESHOLD_MS (drives dashboard
    ghost cleanup only - see US-01).
  end note

  alt now() - last_seen_ms > SIGNAL_LOSS_THRESHOLD_MS
    Evaluator -> AlertState : GET alert-state:{entity_id}

    alt no active alert
      Evaluator -> TSDB : SELECT last known position\nWHERE entity_id = ? ORDER BY timestamp_ms DESC LIMIT 1
      TSDB --> Evaluator : { lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

      Evaluator -> Kafka : publish to alerts\n{ alert_id, alert_type: SIGNAL_LOSS, entity_id,\n  last_known_position, duration_ms }
      Evaluator -> AlertState : SET alert-state:{entity_id} $last_seen_ms\n(value = dark_since_ms; no TTL - cleared by position consumer on entity resume)

    else alert already active
      Evaluator -> Evaluator : skip - suppressed by alert-state key\nsee alert-suppression diagram
    end

  else entity seen within threshold
    Evaluator -> Evaluator : no action
  end
end

@enduml
